+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"Done. The versioned document store is implemented in `src/index.ts` with full CRUD, version history, branching, and three-way structural merging.\n\n**Implementation** (`src/index.ts`)\n- `DocumentStoreImpl` class + `createDocumentStore()` factory, exporting the `DocumentStore` interface along with `Version`, `Conflict`, and `MergeResult` types.\n- Each branch holds its own `documents` map and per-document `histories` (version arrays). `create`/`update` push a new `Version` (UUID + timestamp + deep-cloned content).\n- `createBranch` deep-copies the source branch's documents and histories, and records a merge-base snapshot for the new branch pair (inheriting relationships with third branches so multi-branch merges stay correct).\n- `merge(sourceBranch)` iterates the union of base/ours/theirs document IDs and delegates to `mergeDocument`, which handles create/delete/modify at the document level and recurses into `mergeField` for structural field-level three-way merge.\n\n**Merge semantics**\n- Three-way: compares both branches against the stored common-ancestor snapshot. Only-one-side-changed → take that side; both-same-value → no conflict; both-different → conflict.\n- Nested objects merge field-by-field (conflicts report dot-paths like `obj.p`); arrays are treated as opaque leaf values.\n- Document-level create/delete/modify is handled distinctly from \"never existed\" by checking base presence, so delete-vs-modify is a real conflict while clean deletes/adds merge silently.\n- No conflicts → auto-applied to the current branch and the merge base advances to the source's state. Conflicts → not applied, current branch unchanged, `merged` preview resolves ties in favor of \"ours\".\n\n**Validation**\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, `npx eslint src/ tests/` clean.\n- 30 tests in `tests/store.test.ts` covering CRUD, deep-clone isolation, version history, branch isolation, fast-forward, independent doc/field merges, conflicts, nested paths, arrays, delete/modify-vs-delete, and merge-base advancement — all passing.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: I treat arrays as opaque values (any change replaces the whole array) rather than element-wise, since the spec only guarantees structural merging for objects. If you'd prefer array element-level merging, that's a straightforward extension to `mergeField`."}}
